        "number": "01",
        "numberLabel": "RULE 01",
        "title": "Contrast with Purpose",
        "titleItalic": "Not Chaos",
        "body": "Pair fonts that differ in weight or structure, but share a similar mood. Random contrast creates visual noise, not harmony.",
        "quote": "Difference should clarify, not compete."
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-typo-sample",
      "slots": {
        "pageOf": "3 / 8",
        "authorInitials": "TK",
        "authorName": "TypeKit",
        "handle": "@typekit",
        "avatarBg1": "#d65f3e",
        "avatarBg2": "#f7f2ea",
        "number": "02",
        "numberLabel": "RULE 02",
        "title": "Limit Your Font",
        "titleItalic": "Families",
        "body": "Use two typefaces maximum for any layout. A third font is only justified when you need a distinct accent for data or code.",
        "quote": "Restraint is the mark of a pro."
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-typo-sample",
      "slots": {
        "pageOf": "4 / 8",
        "authorInitials": "TK",
        "authorName": "TypeKit",
        "handle": "@typekit",
        "avatarBg1": "#d65f3e",
        "avatarBg2": "#f7f2ea",
        "number": "03",
        "numberLabel": "RULE 03",
        "title": "Match the Mood",
        "titleItalic": "Exactly",
        "body": "A playful script clashes with a stern slab serif. Check the era and tone of both fonts before you commit to the marriage.",
        "quote": "Tone is invisible but deafening."
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-typo-sample",
      "slots": {
        "pageOf": "5 / 8",
        "authorInitials": "TK",
        "authorName": "TypeKit",
        "handle": "@typekit",
        "avatarBg1": "#d65f3e",
        "avatarBg2": "#f7f2ea",
        "number": "04",
        "numberLabel": "RULE 04",
        "title": "Give Every Font",
        "titleItalic": "One Job",
        "body": "Assign clear roles to each typeface. Let one command attention as the display face while the other serves quiet duty for reading body copy.",
        "quote": "Hierarchy lives in division of labor."
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-typo-sample",
      "slots": {
        "pageOf": "6 / 8",
        "authorInitials": "TK",
        "authorName": "TypeKit",
        "handle": "@typekit",
        "avatarBg1": "#d65f3e",
        "avatarBg2": "#f7f2ea",
        "number": "05",
        "numberLabel": "RULE 05",
        "title": "Check Your Lowercase",
        "titleItalic": "Heights",
        "body": "If lowercase letters sit at wildly different heights, your text will feel bumpy. Align the x-height for seamless pairing across sizes.",
        "quote": "The baseline is a promise."
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-typo-sample",
      "slots": {
        "pageOf": "7 / 8",
        "authorInitials": "TK",
        "authorName": "TypeKit",
        "handle": "@typekit",
        "avatarBg1": "#d65f3e",
        "avatarBg2": "#f7f2ea",
        "number": "06",
        "numberLabel": "RULE 06",
        "title": "Test at Every",
        "titleItalic": "Size",
        "body": "A pairing that sings at poster scale may crumble in captions. Scale your test from thumbnail to billboard before shipping the final file.",
        "quote": "Context is the final critic."
      }
    },
